@startuml option_c_hybrid
title Option C — static KG summary + KG tools available

actor User
participant "ask.py\n(CLI)" as CLI
participant "LangGraph\nagent loop" as Agent
participant "KG context loader" as Loader
participant "LLM\n(Gemini)" as LLM
participant "MCP server" as MCP
participant "Fusion tools" as FusionTools
participant "KG tools" as KGTools
participant "OracleClient" as OracleClient
participant "FusionClient" as FusionClient
participant "Oracle 26ai" as Oracle
participant "Fusion REST" as FusionPod

== Startup ==
Agent -> Loader : load_kg_summary()
Loader -> OracleClient : minimal SELECTs
OracleClient -> Oracle : SQL
Oracle --> OracleClient : rows
OracleClient --> Loader : KG
Loader --> Agent : kg_summary (short)

== Per-request ==
User -> CLI : prompt
CLI -> Agent : run_agent(prompt)
Agent -> MCP : load_mcp_tools()
MCP --> Agent : Fusion tools + KG tools (BOTH)

Agent -> LLM : SYSTEM = base + kg_summary\nUSER = prompt\nTOOLS = Fusion + KG
note right of LLM
  LLM has KG basics always.
  Can call KG tools for more.
end note

LLM --> Agent : tool_call: search_suppliers_by_country("US")
Agent -> MCP : invoke
MCP -> FusionTools : ...
FusionTools -> FusionClient : GET
FusionClient -> FusionPod : HTTPS
FusionPod --> FusionClient : suppliers
FusionClient --> FusionTools : suppliers
FusionTools --> MCP : suppliers
MCP --> Agent : suppliers
Agent -> LLM : updated context

LLM --> Agent : tool_call: kg_get_pattern("no_Y_in_N_months")
note right of LLM
  LLM wants more details
  about the pattern than
  the summary provides
end note
Agent -> MCP : invoke
MCP -> KGTools : kg_get_pattern(...)
KGTools -> OracleClient : SQL
OracleClient -> Oracle : SQL
Oracle --> OracleClient : pattern
OracleClient --> KGTools : pattern
KGTools --> MCP : pattern
MCP --> Agent : pattern
Agent -> LLM : updated context

note over LLM, Agent
  Mix of Fusion calls and
  KG drill-down calls follow.
end note

LLM --> Agent : final_answer
Agent --> CLI : answer text
CLI --> User : printed answer
@enduml